            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is not really an issue with 'mini.align' but with how extmarks with virtual text work in Neovim. The 'mini.align' uses `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines()` to set new aligned content of lines (even if it is the same). This in turn affects placed extmarks as if current text is removed completely and the new one is then pasted/typed. *This* in turn makes extmark move to the right because it by default has `right_gravity` set to `false`.\n\nThe same behavior can be replicated by executing `:lua vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, 1, true, { \"new line\" })` instead of `ga_<Space>`.\n\nThere is nothing 'mini.align' can do here. The real solution here, I'd say, is to add `right_gravity = false` to the extmark options.\n\nClosing as not really an issue with 'mini.align'.",
